/*
  MaskedValue.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0220 · MaskedValue (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. The web source
  (components/ui/MaskedValue.tsx) resolves its three interactive labels through `t(key, default)`: the
  reveal / hide toggle label (which mirrors the current state) and the copy button's accessible label.
  Native ships NO hardcoded prose, so those keys are resolved through the P1/S10 facade
  (MaskedValueStrings). The `value` and `ariaLabel` props are caller-supplied (already-localized) string
  props, so they carry no key here — and the `ariaLabel`, never the raw secret, is what VoiceOver reads.

  All keys live in the per-surface "MaskedValue" table and fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings`
  master catalog at integration time. In test / preview bundles `NSLocalizedString` returns the value
  below, keeping the default render deterministic and byte-identical to the web English copy.
*/

/* --- Toggle labels (web t('mask.reveal') / t('mask.hide'), mirrored to the revealed state) --- */

/* Shown on the eye toggle while the value is masked — tap to reveal the cleartext. */
"mask.reveal" = "Reveal value";

/* Shown on the eye toggle while the value is revealed — tap to mask it again. */
"mask.hide" = "Hide value";

/* --- Copy button (web t('mask.copy'), the iconOnly CopyButton's accessible label) --- */

/* The accessible label of the copy button, which always copies the raw value regardless of mask state. */
"mask.copy" = "Copy value";
